# dict_key_no_ihash.tkr — the fase1b KEY-GATE reject host. It proves `Dictionary`/`HashSet`'s key
# constraint `K: IEq & IHash` is a REAL compile-time gate: a key type that conforms `IEq` but not
# `IHash` (here `Plain`) cannot instantiate the hash-scan helper `dict_find_index<K: IEq & IHash>`.
# A self-contained project (its own IEq/IHash/NeByEq copies, since teko::cmp is compiler-internal).
# It has no successful build to sanitize/run (EXPECT_COMPILE_FAIL).

Feature: dict_key_no_ihash — the K: IEq & IHash key gate rejects a non-IHash key at instantiation

  Scenario: key_without_ihash_rejected — Plain (IEq, no IHash) cannot key the hash-scan gate
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "does not satisfy its constraint"
